      "writtenOn": "2024-11-22T12:50:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC the idea of the APIs is that they can be implemented by (external) clients that talk to Gerrit servers. In this case the client can extend the NotImplemented classes so that it continues to work when we extend the API with new methods.\n\nMaybe that idea didn\u0027t get much traction, but there is the gerrit-rest-java-client [1] that is using this approach [2] and this client seems to be still maintained [3]. So it looks like this is still used and removing these classes would break that client?\n\nIs there an actual issue with having these classes, besides needing to add a trivial method to them, when we extend the API? I.e. why not just keep them?\n\n[1] https://github.com/uwolfer/gerrit-rest-java-client\n[2] https://github.com/uwolfer/gerrit-rest-java-client/blob/master/src/main/java/com/urswolfer/gerrit/client/rest/http/changes/ChangeApiRestClient.java#L39\n[3] https://github.com/uwolfer/gerrit-rest-java-client/commits/master/",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 9,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "39fcfc8f01301908b4c20d041e7cde4d34dc57a0",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0f353aad_5b327241",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
